Done. Both changes build cleanly, pass the existing test suite, and behave correctly end-to-end.

**`src/lib.rs`** — added `filter_by_tag`:
```rust
pub fn filter_by_tag<'a>(notes: &'a [Note], tag: &str) -> Vec<&'a Note> {
    notes
        .iter()
        .filter(|n| n.tags.iter().any(|t| t == tag))
        .collect()
}
```
Exact match via `==` (not substring), order preserved by iteration.

**`src/main.rs`** — the `list` command now accepts `--tag <TAG>`: it scans the remaining args, and when `--tag` is present, routes output through `filter_by_tag` (cloning the matched `&Note`s back into a `Vec<Note>`); otherwise it lists all notes as before. Added `filter_by_tag` and `Note` to the `use notekeep::{...}` import.

Verified with scratch data: `--tag rust` returns exactly the notes tagged `rust` in relative order; `rustic`/`ru` (substring) and an unmatched tag return nothing. All scratch files removed afterward.


